   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## A rough clip in, a finished video out\n\n**kubakub motion guide (ltx)** takes a moving clip and lets LTX repaint it. What moves, where and when stays yours; how it looks comes from the prompt.\n\nHere the guide is a **kubakub shader** (*depth scan*: a sheet of light travelling through the sample facade). Use instead:\n\n- the **frames** of a **kubakub director sequence** (your layers, masks, lamps, shader fills, in time with your sound)\n- a previz from **scene walkthrough** or your own 3D render\n- any clip from Load Video\n\n**repaint** is the one number that matters: **0.91** repaints everything and still follows the guide. Higher (0.95 - 0.98) is freer, lower (0.7) keeps the guide's own look. At 1 the guide is ignored. Say in the prompt what moves, the same as in the guide.\n\n**Where and when:** connect a mask to **repaint_mask** (white = the repaint shows, black = the guide stays exactly; one mask per frame makes the repaint travel, for example from kubakub mask animate) and pick a **curve** (ramp = from your guide to fully repainted; beats = with the sound).\n\nSmall moving things can get lost: make them big and bright in the guide. On a 12 GB card: 0.2 megapixels, up to 121 frames. Bypass the upscaler (node 14) for a fast first look.\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
